⍝ ZZ69_Regression.tc
⍝ ══════════════════

      ⍝ bug-apl@gnu.org, "GNU APL analysis 22" (Blake McBride, 2026-08-20),
      ⍝ findings #4 and #5: regression coverage for the printer stack-
      ⍝ overflow and the packed-ravel exactness findings. See SVN log for
      ⍝ details; findings #1/#2/#3/#6/#7 from the same report are covered
      ⍝ in Residue.tc, Domino_stress.tc, Circle_Functions.tc, Quad_JSON.tc
      ⍝ and Quad_XML.tc respectively.

      )CLEAR
CLEAR WS

      ⍝ #4: displaying (⎕← or ⍕) a sufficiently deeply nested value used
      ⍝ to SIGSEGV the interpreter via unbounded mutual recursion between
      ⍝ PrintBuffer::PrintBuffer() and PointerCell::character_
      ⍝ representation(), with no depth counter or limit anywhere in that
      ⍝ recursion. Two independent layers now guard against this:
      ⍝
      ⍝ 1. PointerCell's constructor -- the single chokepoint every
      ⍝    nesting-increasing construction (⊂, strand notation, indexed/
      ⍝    selective/member assignment, ...) funnels through -- refuses to
      ⍝    nest a value one level deeper than MAX_DEPTH (254), raising
      ⍝    SYSTEM LIMIT (nesting depth) immediately, during construction,
      ⍝    rather than only failing later when eventually printed.
      ⍝
      ⍝ 2. PrintBuffer::MAX_PRINT_NESTING_DEPTH (500), the original fix,
      ⍝    remains as defense in depth for any value that reaches the
      ⍝    printer via a path other than PointerCell (e.g. workspace
      ⍝    deserialisation); it is no longer reachable from ordinary APL
      ⍝    construction now that layer 1 stops it 246 levels earlier.
      ⍝
∇Z←DEEP N;I
 Z←1 2
 I←0
L: I←I+1
 →(I>N)/0
 Z←⊂Z
 →L
∇
      ⍝ exactly at the limit (depth 254) still succeeds; not printed here
      ⍝ (a 254-deep box is enormous) -- printing a shallow value is
      ⍝ covered separately below.
      ⍝
      W←DEEP 253
      ≡W
254
      )ERASE W

      ⍝ one level deeper (depth 255) is refused during construction --
      ⍝ V is never assigned, long before any print is attempted
      ⍝
      V←DEEP 254
SYSTEM LIMIT (nesting depth)
DEEP[5]  Z←⊂Z
           ^
      )SIC

      ⎕←V
VALUE ERROR+
      ⎕←V
        ^
      )SIC

      ⍝ a value safely under the limit must still print normally
      ⍝
      X←DEEP 5
      6≡≡X
1
      )ERASE X DEEP

      )SIC
      )CHECK
OK      - no stale functions
OK      - no stale values
OK      - no stale indices
OK      - no duplicate parents

      ⍝ #5: Value::try_pack() escalated a ravel mixing exact IntCells
      ⍝ and FloatCells to a packed RPT_FLOAT64 ravel, silently demoting
      ⍝ every exact IntCell to a double -- observable once the ravel
      ⍝ length crosses ⎕SYL[34;2] (the packing threshold), since a
      ⍝ shorter, otherwise-identical ravel stays unpacked (mixed Cell
      ⍝ storage) and keeps each cell's own correct type. V and W below
      ⍝ differ only in length (11 vs 12 elements): both contain the same
      ⍝ first element (20÷1, an exact integer 20), but only W's length
      ⍝ reaches the default packing threshold of 12.
      ⍝
      ⎕SYL[34;2]
12
      V←20÷⍳11
      W←20÷⍳12
      V[1]≡W[1]
1
      (!V[1]) ≡ !W[1]
1
      !W[1]
2432902008176640000
      )ERASE V W

      )SIC
      )CHECK
OK      - no stale functions
OK      - no stale values
OK      - no stale indices
OK      - no duplicate parents

      )CLEAR
CLEAR WS

      ]NEXTFILE
